  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study on offshore wind R&amp;D opportunities for The Netherlands in the United States of America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This study researches how Dutch expertise in offshore wind energy can be linked to the research and development opportunities in the United States of America (USA), in line with the American sustainability and energy objectives described in the Research and Development (R&amp;D) roadmap 4.0 of the American National Offshore Wind Research and Development Consortium (NOWRDC). The main goal of the study, funded by CERF, is to promote a long-term collaboration in the field of innovation between the USA and the Netherlands. This collaboration is aimed at realising the American objective to install 30 gigawatts of offshore wind energy by 2030 with the support of Dutch innovations in offshore wind. The study serves as the foundation for the innovation mission scheduled from 23-25 October 2024, to Massachusetts and Rhode Island, involving Dutch research institutes, maritime contractors, and suppliers.RemarkDue to the transparency with regard to the IATI projects, a non-ODA country has been included in this project.</narrative>
  </description>
